The executable controller, runner, validator and evaluation adapters are copied byte for byte in frozen_sources/ with repository-relative paths. frozen_controller.py, frozen_run.py and frozen_validate.py provide convenient top-level copies. The archive has 490 source/metadata files (20,014,509 bytes), including 472 actually loaded native source files across the independently named semantic, world-memory and context profiles. loaded_source_manifest.json is independent of live module paths and records each original path, saved path, role and SHA-256.

Run the read-only archived audit from any working directory with `.venv/bin/python /absolute/path/to/development-v2/audit_archived.py development-v2`. It reads the actual retained ledger/effect/output artifacts and resolves source hashes to archived source bytes, so later changes to live controller.py or its adapters do not invalidate this evidence review. Its 9,188 checks pass. The original validator remains copied unchanged; audit_archived.py is a separately identified path-resolving audit, not a changed outcome or native-runtime substitute.

A new execution requires a newly frozen output profile with source paths remapped to the selected archived runtime; do not overwrite this run. The code copies preserve the implementation for that reconstruction. The Docker image is pinned but not exported, and the Python runtime, non-code package resources and full context-store environment still need to be available/reconstructed. Standalone execution from only this source archive has not been qualified. No historical snapshots were changed.
